      "standardized_narrative": "The syndicate reported a gross prior year reserve release of $142.1 million, representing a 3.94% release of opening gross claims outstanding. This release is primarily attributed to the gradual release of the management margin as best estimates mature, in line with the reserving policy. While the syndicate had previously maintained explicit reserve uplifts for high inflation, the current year's movement reflects a release. Prior year events such as Hurricane Ian (2022), the Russia/Ukraine conflict (2022), Hurricane Ida (2021), Winter Storm Uri (2021), European floods (2021), Kentucky tornadoes (2021), and COVID-19 (2020) would have influenced the underlying reserve estimates that are now being released.",
      "raw_causal_phrases": [
        "As the best estimate matures and becomes more certain, the management margin is gradually released in line with the reserving policy.",
        "The Syndicate maintains explicit reserve uplifts to allow for the impact of high inflation in recent years."
      ],
